# sha256 of every tarball the fork's images/nginx/rootfs/download.sh fetches
# with get_src, keyed by the URL exactly as written there (before its version
# variables from version.sh are expanded). The fork ships stale checksums and
# has the check commented out; source.sh puts these in their place and turns
# the check back on, so a moved tag or a version bump in version.sh fails the
# build until the entry here is updated. See README.md, "Changing what is built".
